WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:05.520
It's 6,371 kilometres to the centre
of the Earth.

00:00:05.560 --> 00:00:06.920
Follow us down.

00:00:06.960 --> 00:00:09.760
We're going all the way
to the heart of the planet.

00:00:14.160 --> 00:00:18.080
Our world is made of layers,
a bit like an onion,

00:00:18.120 --> 00:00:22.320
and as far as we know, life only
exists in the first layer -

00:00:22.360 --> 00:00:26.040
the crust. In the crust, you'll find
the burrows of animals

00:00:26.080 --> 00:00:28.160
such as moles and badgers.

00:00:28.200 --> 00:00:32.040
The deepest are made by
Nile crocodiles

00:00:32.080 --> 00:00:34.320
and can reach depths of 12 metres.

00:00:34.360 --> 00:00:38.080
The crust is also home to ancient
underground cities

00:00:38.120 --> 00:00:39.800
like Elengubu in Turkey,

00:00:39.840 --> 00:00:44.440
an elaborate labyrinth capable of
housing 20,000 people,

00:00:44.480 --> 00:00:46.440
complete with schools and chapels.

00:00:46.480 --> 00:00:50.960
It is thought to have been built
around 370 years BC.

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:55.080
The world's deepest mines can go
down to around four kilometres.

00:00:55.120 --> 00:00:59.760
South African gold miners have found
worms two kilometres down,

00:00:59.800 --> 00:01:02.720
but all life stops before
three kilometres.

00:01:02.760 --> 00:01:06.560
Then there's the deepest hole
ever drilled -

00:01:06.600 --> 00:01:09.200
the Kola Superdeep Borehole
in Russia.

00:01:09.240 --> 00:01:11.680
Some call it the gateway to hell,

00:01:11.720 --> 00:01:15.680
with locals claiming to hear
the screams of tortured souls.

00:01:15.720 --> 00:01:18.960
At around 30 to 50 kilometres depth,

00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:21.600
we reach the next layer -
the mantle.

00:01:21.640 --> 00:01:25.400
It's made of hot rock, which appears
solid to us

00:01:25.440 --> 00:01:30.320
but actually flows very slowly,
just a few centimetres a year.

00:01:30.360 --> 00:01:35.400
These delicate shifts below can give
rise to earthquakes above.

00:01:35.440 --> 00:01:39.440
In the 1960s, a group of scientists
attempted to drill

00:01:39.480 --> 00:01:41.440
into the Earth's mantle.

00:01:41.480 --> 00:01:45.640
Although unsuccessful, new efforts
are afoot with a plan to drill

00:01:45.680 --> 00:01:48.560
deep below the Indian Ocean.

00:01:48.600 --> 00:01:50.880
As we descend, the increasing
pressure

00:01:50.920 --> 00:01:53.640
means that atoms become warped,

00:01:53.680 --> 00:01:56.920
and even the most familiar materials
behave bizarrely.

00:01:56.960 --> 00:02:00.400
Crystals change from green to blue
to brown,

00:02:00.440 --> 00:02:04.240
and rock becomes as malleable
as plastic.

00:02:04.280 --> 00:02:08.720
2,900 kilometres down, we reach
the bottom of the mantle.

00:02:08.760 --> 00:02:10.720
See those two giant blobs?

00:02:10.760 --> 00:02:13.280
They're the size of continents.

00:02:13.320 --> 00:02:18.160
Scientists aren't sure how they were
formed or what they're made of.

00:02:18.200 --> 00:02:21.400
They cradle the next layer -
the outer core.

00:02:21.440 --> 00:02:25.400
In Jules Verne's classic novel,
Journey to the Center of the Earth,

00:02:25.440 --> 00:02:29.360
Professor Otto Lidenbrock encounters
an entire underground world,

00:02:29.400 --> 00:02:33.600
replete with prehistoric creatures
and a subterranean ocean.

00:02:33.640 --> 00:02:36.520
While the dinosaurs might
have been a bit of a stretch,

00:02:36.560 --> 00:02:38.720
there is an ocean of sorts,

00:02:38.760 --> 00:02:42.640
but this one consists of flowing
red-hot iron and nickel,

00:02:42.680 --> 00:02:47.280
a sunless sea with its own currents
and jet streams.

00:02:47.320 --> 00:02:51.200
This motion creates a magnetic field
that protects the Earth

00:02:51.240 --> 00:02:53.560
from dangerous solar rays.

00:02:53.600 --> 00:02:57.360
The final layer is known
as the inner core.

00:02:57.400 --> 00:03:00.680
It's 6,000 degrees in here.

00:03:00.720 --> 00:03:04.920
The pressure is so intense
that the metals here

00:03:04.960 --> 00:03:08.280
have crystallised, forming
a solid sphere

00:03:08.320 --> 00:03:10.640
at the very centre of our planet.

00:03:12.040 --> 00:03:15.360
In reality, our little vehicle
would have been crushed

00:03:15.400 --> 00:03:17.800
and melted long ago.

00:03:17.840 --> 00:03:21.360
And as for our driver, I think
she better head back to the surface.

00:03:21.400 --> 00:03:23.320
It's a long way to go.

00:03:23.360 --> 00:03:24.800
Good luck!

